SELECT 122, 116, 47, 3, 'I had to ask the waitress twice " where is the crab pictured on the menu?" She replied that they didn''t have that crab on the menu. The crab pictured was a blue crab indigenous to the Rappahannock and the Potomac river which are both close to Fredericksburg VA. I would suggest that Joe change the name to Snow Crab Shack or King Crab Shack because he has no Blue Crabs. After learning the sad truth I settled for a Snow Crab bucket with corn and potatoes which was good. Service was good. Bathrooms not well marked but clean and modern. Bar well stocked and a good happy hour that I missed.', '2019-10-25 02:29:26', NULL
