SELECT 718, 666, 35, 5, 'I heard a lot of good things about this place so I wanted to check it out. It was not as crowded as I thought it would be. But be aware that parking can be difficult. I didn''t see a parking lot here and I parked on the street. So I imagine if it gets busy it might be hard to find a spot. I ordered the Mac and cheese with pulled pork and my friend got a brisket sandwich. One of the main things that stood out to me here is everyone is so friendly! From the person greeting me when I walked in, the person taking my order, making my food, checking me out at the end, and even when I went to leave. They told me "we hope you had a great time and we hope you come back!". Everyone there made the experience great. The food was good and my friend said it was the best brisket she''s had and that the espresso BBQ sauce was perfect. I can''t even say that I have a complaint but I do have a suggestion. They have a lot of different bbq sauces from espresso BBQ, to vinegar, to a house made. I would just really like to see a sweeter sauce. I know living so close to Carolina I''m going to find a lot of vinegar style sauces. But I do enjoy a sweeter sauce. The house one is ok but for me it was still a little on the vinegar side. Either way I will definitely be back!', '2019-07-27 19:42:40', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 719, 667, 35, 3, 'I ordered the brisket platter and pulled chicken sandwich with beans macaroni and cheese greens and the banana pudding the tast of the brisket good the greens were a bit spicy the beans had a unique taste but edible macaroni and cheese was different and pulled chicken was good banana pudding was a hit and the little piece of cornbread was very yummy!!!', '2020-07-23 00:18:33', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 720, 668, 35, 2, 'Food was OK but the price of the food is a joke 3 pcs of beef brisket and 4 bones of ribs and some fries for 42 dollars Are you serious', '2021-04-27 23:51:17', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 721, 669, 35, 5, 'Very good food, we ordered the brisket sandwhich platter with Mac and cheese and cole slaw as well as the pulled pork sandwhich with baked beans and collards. Eveything was delicious. Corn bread and banana pudding was pretty good as well. I''ll definitely be back to try more!', '2021-02-18 04:00:59', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 722, 670, 35, 4, 'First time trying Redwood Smoke Shack. Food was flavorful and tender. We got the meat sweats platter which comes with 2 bones, pulled chicken, pulled pork, brisket, pickled onions, jalapenos, pickles, cornbread and 2 sides. We got mac n cheese and baked beans. The mac n cheese was average and the baked beans were delicious! The cornbread was how I like it moist with a hint of sweetness.  We also got burnt ends which was very good as well. You can make it into a platter,  but I choose not to because I wanted the corn and that wasn''t offered as a side. The corn was amazing! They slather some creamy cilantro sauce on it after it''s been roasted. I absolutely loved it. The customer service is awesome. Very friendly people. They have a sink next to the drink machine, which I loved because it''s bbq, so of course your hands are going to get dirty. There is indoor and patio seating.  6 tables inside and 8 outside. The flies were a both at the outdoor tables but that''s to be expected. They have rolls of paper towels at some of the tables and sauce trays. The sauces were okay. But I personally didn''t need sauce on my meats because it was seasoned perfectly well. Next time I''m going to try the pulled chicken sammich with cole slaw.', '2019-07-26 22:49:10', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 723, 671, 35, 1, 'Ordered the Meat Sweets Platter several times. The first two times platters were very good. I saved some of the platters to eat later. Food was still fresh after I microwaved food. I ordered again and platters were horrible. The ribs were not fresh and burnt. The Slaw wasn''t like the first two times. Your platters are expensive so you should bring it in every time you sell them. I don''t know if there are several different  people cooking and preparing your food but notice different taste in seasonings cooking. I was looking for consistency. I''m very disappointed for what I paid for.', '2020-09-28 18:46:43', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 724, 672, 35, 5, 'Fabulous TX brisket.  Great mac and collard greens sides, and dessert sweet cornbread.  Have a beer, sit outside and savor the moment.', '2020-11-22 01:09:38', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 725, 673, 35, 5, 'Great authentic BBQ! Finally got a chance to try this place and it did not disappoint! The smoked meats were great and the sides were ok but not bad being open only a week. I absolutely love seeing a smoker out back too. If youre in the mood for some good barbecue then check this place out.', '2019-06-29 19:33:34', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 726, 674, 35, 5, 'This is the business that replaced the Dog N Burger joint 3 years ago which we enjoyed. So I suggested to my husband that we should try that place out since we were in the area. So glad that he obliged me. OMG their food was so delicious! We ordered 2 lunch specials,the pulled chicken and the cheddar jalapeno one with sides. (beans, collards and corn pudding) And our desserts were banana misu and bread pudding. Also washed it all down with some delicious sweet tea. We will definitely patronize that place again in the future.', '2020-11-06 14:40:51', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 727, 670, 35, 4, 'First time trying Redwood Smoke Shack. Food was flavorful and tender. We got the meat sweats platter which comes with 2 bones, pulled chicken, pulled pork, brisket, pickled onions, jalapenos, pickles, cornbread and 2 sides. We got mac n cheese and baked beans. The mac n cheese was average and the baked beans were delicious! The cornbread was how I like it moist with a hint of sweetness.  We also got burnt ends which was very good as well. You can make it into a platter,  but I choose not to because I wanted the corn and that wasn''t offered as a side. The corn was amazing! They slather some creamy cilantro sauce on it after it''s been roasted. I absolutely loved it. The customer service is awesome. Very friendly people. They have a sink next to the drink machine, which I loved because it''s bbq, so of course your hands are going to get dirty. There is indoor and patio seating.  6 tables inside and 8 outside. The flies were a both at the outdoor tables but that''s to be expected. They have rolls of paper towels at some of the tables and sauce trays. The sauces were okay. But I personally didn''t need sauce on my meats because it was seasoned perfectly well. Next time I''m going to try the pulled chicken sammich with cole slaw.', '2019-07-26 22:49:10', NULL
UNION ALL
