UNION ALL
SELECT 2160, 2067, 10, 5, '4.5 stars, rounded up for the décor and waitstaff. Clearly many folks posting reviews thus far don''t know what they are getting into. Great Tapas place with some of the best service in CVille and a great mix of flavors and unique presentations. Highlights from our meal were the pork loin and lamb dishes; the bar menu is a work in progress but our Malbec was decent for the price and the Islay Dusk cocktail was excellent. Will go back to see how they grow', '2019-03-09 03:29:03', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 2161, 2068, 10, 2, 'Little Star is where Threepenny Cafe used to be. With its warm energy, and kind staff, the restaurant welcomes you but after that, everything is subpar. At that price point, with all the hype, we expected to find more than a menu of dishes that were either too flat in taste and looks or too overwhelmed with some type of ingredient like mustard, mayo or cheese. We were expecting an elegant delicacy from the trio of Chef Ryan Collins, Chef Tristan Wraight and Ben Clore, yet found nothing close to what they can potentially offer. You would be much better off going to Oakhart Social or Más for a delicious fare. I am not sure what Chef José Andrés would think of these dishes but I certainly hope that we stop the slew of restaurants that offer blend food at big city prices. Charlottesville deserves better.', '2019-01-04 14:21:33', NULL
UNION ALL
