SELECT 7053, 6769, 43, 5, 'Great food, great service. Love this subway!', '2017-02-08 23:58:51', NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT 7054, 6770, 43, 3, 'Staff have always been nice to me (Hi Maria and Arsu!) and they are pretty quick too (and food tastes fresh) and I planned to do a great review and survey for them...but there have been a couple of mistakes/bad decisions: I bought a sub yesterday and toward the end of the sub there was a different taste, somewhat like a chemical.  I had extreme pain and was in the bathroom for an hour approx 3 hrs after buying the meal and I hadnt ingested anything else.  So, Im guessing it was a cleaning agent that dripped into one of the food containers...something like that.   The other issue was that I was in line at an angle casually since I wasnt getting a sandwich per se/didnt need to see ingredients and there was only 1 purchaser ahead of me and otherwise an empty store.  As I approached at an angle from the drink machine, another person entered the store.  I remained behind the guy in front of me and kept moving as the line moved.  Yet, the large guy (tall, looked pregnant, kind of looked like a mix of spanish and white but super ugly with bad attire and grooming) who walked in kept walking bit by bit as if to try to block me but he didnt entirely so I figured he understood and respected that I was in line. They dont hire people to stand closely behind random customers in lines..so duhh. Then when the nice cashier guy said "Yes maam" the large guy sped up and walked directly in front of me blocking me!  I said "Wow that was really inconsiderate...whatever go ahead"  He was like "What??" I said "I was already here before you arrived..I''ve been standing here" He said I wasnt positioned in an exact line and it was ignorant of me not to speak up.  Sure, if I spoke up he probably would have gotten confrontational about THAT and I try to avoid such things.  I mostly dont fault the cashier but then again he could have told the guy he had to help me first.  This has happened to me multiple times in the Alexandria area - while standing exactly straight in a line - but its usually a cashier who omits me.  A lot of selfish disrespectful (racist?) a-holes out here...then you get sweetie pies too...its like people trend strongly one way or the other. :/ Leaving when I can.  :)', '2016-09-03 23:57:59', NULL
UNION ALL
