SELECT 7171, 6882, 14, 4, 'Recently renovated, it''s a quaint restaurant with tattoo-laden staff who serve coffee, breakfast, lunch, beer, and wine. I ordered chicken salad sandwich, which was fantastic. Came with a side salad equally nice. I ordered a local virginia beer, which I had never heard of, so that was an epiphany. Prices were reasonable, not cheap but not expensive.  Plenty of seating when I went at noon.  Lake Anne is probably the oldest neighborhood in Reston, so it''s not the hotspot anymore but was probably the coolest scene in town back in the 70''s. Worth a visit.', '2017-09-11 19:40:07', NULL
UNION ALL
