SELECT 14557, 13386, 6, 2, 'I went here for a birthday luncheon. The staff was very friendly and our waitress was very attentive. I had a burger, which was pretty good, nothing special. The menu was interesting in that they have crab legs and lobster, which many other steak restaurants in the area don''t have. I would be interested to go back and try some of the dinner entrees, although some seemed to be a little pricey. I didn''t really have a problem with the decor. It wasn''t anything special. There were some peanut shells on the floor, but I''ve seen the same at other steak restaurants, as well as places like 5 Guys. Overall, it seems like an average steak place. More observations after my next visit. Update: 2nd visit was not as good. I had a very thin and very dry steak sandwich, which, I mistakenly thought I was ordering a burger. I could tell the fries had been cooked in old grease and they tasted horribly. The waitress kindly replaced them with some mac and cheese, which was much better, albeit tasting like something off the children''s menu. I was unimpressed after my first visit and this had lowered my opinion further. I do not expect to return.', '2014-09-26 20:36:50', NULL
UNION ALL
